   "id": "P5",
   "type": "proposition",
   "name": null,
   "statement": "$A$ and $B$ are two distinct points on a line $AB$. $C_0$ and $C_1$ are two distinct points on a line $C$. $A \\neq C_0$, and $|AB| > |C_0C_1|$. There must be a point $E$ between $A$ and $B$, s.t., $|AE| = |C_0C_1|$",
