   "statement": "$AB$ and $CD$ are two different lines intersecting at $E$. $A$ and $B$ are two distinct points on $AB$. $C$ and $D$ are two distinct points on $CD$. $E$ is between $A$ and $B$, and $E$ is also between $C$ and $D$. Then, we have $\\angle~AEC = \\angle~DEB$ and $\\angle~CEB = \\angle~AED$.",
   "origin": "paper",
