   "statement": "$A$ and $A'$ are two disctinct points on a line $AA'$. $B$ and $B'$ are two distinct points on a line $BB'$. $C$ and $C'$ are two distinct points on a line $CC'$. $|AA'| + |BB'|~>~|CC'|$, $|AA'| + |CC'|~>~|BB'|$, and $|BB'| + |CC'|~>~|AA'|$. Then, there must exist $\\triangle~KFG$, s.t., $|FK| = |AA'|$, $|FG| = |BB'|$, and $|KG| = |CC'|$.",
